k falls from {sun:Hyde Park|6-21|10:00}% at 10:00 to {sun:Hyde Park|6-21|14:00}% at 14:00 as the towers to the west take over."},{"title":"Where the heights come from","provenance":true,"date":[9,22],"from":"15:00","to":"15:30","hold":9,"cam":[-1200,-1900,900],"tgt":[-250,-500,40],"text":"Blue: surveyed, published or verified height. Orange: floor count \u00d7 storey height. Green: estimated. Against {acc:matched} published tower heights the median error is {acc:median_abs_error_pct}%."},{"title":"After dark","text":"Windows light from the same facade grid that shades them by day. Drag to explore, or open Sun access to test a tower of your own.","cam":[900,1900,700],"tgt":[-200,-350,40],"date":[9,22],"from":"19:05","to":"19:50","hold":10}],"start":{"date":[3,21],"time":"08:40","cam":[2600,3200,1700],"tgt":[-180,-380,30]},"protection":{"title":"Sydney LEP 2012, clause 6.18","summary":"Development may not add to the total shadow on these public places across their protected hours.","source_note":"Protected windows as amended by Amendment No 64. The NSW legislation site refused automated access, so they were transcribed from secondary sources; check the official text before relying on them. Places without a verified window show sun now but are not tested.","reading_note":"Two readings matter more than any data error. Times: the Standard Time Act 1987 is reported to read times in legal instruments as standard time, which during daylight saving is an hour later on the clock; for Macquarie Place that changes the sun in its window by up to 44 points. Baseline: the clause compares against buildings existing at a fixed date, while this test compares against today's model.","default_time_basis":"standard","tip":"Tip: try the block west of Hyde Park, or just north of Martin Place.","unprotected_label":"not LEP-listed"},"minor_labels":["Customs House","Queen Victoria Building","Town Hall","St Mary's Cathedral"],"place_labels":["Hyde Park","Martin Place","Barangaroo Reserve","Ro